    {
      "id": "interior-regularity-first-formal-classical-setup",
      "type": "ordinary-paragraph",
      "regions": [
        [
          329,
          80,
          210,
          955,
          620
        ]
      ],
      "en": "For our first calculation let us assume that $\\Omega$ has a smooth boundary $\\partial\\Omega$ with unit outward normal $\\bm{\\eta}=(\\eta_1,\\ldots,\\eta_n)$ and that $u$ is a classical solution of\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:interior-regularity-formal-poisson-equation}\n-\\Delta u=f\n\\end{equation}\nin $\\Omega$, and\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:interior-regularity-formal-dirichlet-boundary}\nu=0\n\\end{equation}\non $\\partial\\Omega$. Our goal is to show that (weak) solutions of elliptic problems such as the one above are actually in a ``better\\textquotesingle\\textquotesingle\\ space than $H_0^1(\\Omega)$. In order to prepare for this, we will now estimate the $L^2(\\Omega)$ norm of the matrix of second partials of $u$ in terms of the $H^1(\\Omega)$ norm. Since this is simply a formal calculation, we will proceed as if we already know that $u$ is as smooth as we like.",
      "zh": "第一次计算中, 假设 $\\Omega$ 有光滑边界 $\\partial\\Omega$, 其单位外法向量为 $\\bm{\\eta}=(\\eta_1,\\ldots,\\eta_n)$, 并且 $u$ 是\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:interior-regularity-formal-poisson-equation}\n-\\Delta u=f\n\\end{equation}\n在 $\\Omega$ 中的经典解, 且\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:interior-regularity-formal-dirichlet-boundary}\nu=0\n\\end{equation}\n在 $\\partial\\Omega$ 上成立. 目标是证明, 上述椭圆问题的 (弱) 解实际上属于比 $H_0^1(\\Omega)$ ``更好\\textquotesingle\\textquotesingle\\ 的空间. 为此作准备, 现在用 $H^1(\\Omega)$ 范数估计 $u$ 的二阶偏导数矩阵的 $L^2(\\Omega)$ 范数. 因为这只是形式计算, 将假定已经知道 $u$ 具有任意所需的光滑性.",
      "label": null,
      "render_role": "ordinary-paragraph",
      "source_locations": [
        {
          "pdf_page": 329,
          "printed_page": 319,
          "bbox": [
            31.980547112462006,
            83.9575489576753,
